{"id": "en_car_blizzard_p2", "total": 65.23, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. A massive snowplow barrels down the dark highway directly toward the buried car.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.04}, {"text": "Mark stays completely inside the vehicle because leaving now means certain death in the freezing storm.", "start": 5.62, "end": 9.7}, {"text": "The heavy steel blade scrapes the top of the snowdrift right above the terrified driver.", "start": 10.36, "end": 13.8}, {"text": "The huge machine passes safely by without crushing the small vehicle hidden under the deep drift.", "start": 14.3, "end": 18.04}, {"text": "Mark remembers every crucial survival rule for staying alive trapped in a winter storm.", "start": 18.74, "end": 22.14}, {"text": "One. Stay right with the car since it acts as your ultimate shelter against the cold.", "start": 21.959, "end": 26.06}, {"text": "Rescuers can spot a stationary car in the snow much faster than a wandering person.", "start": 26.62, "end": 29.9}, {"text": "Two. Run the engine for 10 minutes each hour to generate safe warmth inside.", "start": 29.892, "end": 34.32}, {"text": "Always crack a window just a tiny bit to prevent any dangerous air buildup.", "start": 34.94, "end": 37.86}, {"text": "Three. Clear all snow from the exhaust pipe first so deadly carbon monoxide stays out.", "start": 37.57, "end": 42.26}, {"text": "Tie a bright cloth securely to the antenna so search crews spot you quickly.", "start": 42.74, "end": 45.68}, {"text": "Turn on the inside light at night so passing rescue teams can see your position.", "start": 46.28, "end": 48.92}, {"text": "Mark follows every single safety step patiently while waiting out the freezing winter night.", "start": 49.68, "end": 52.98}, {"text": "Morning light finally breaks across the dark highway and rescue vehicles arrive at last.", "start": 53.64, "end": 57.12}, {"text": "Staying with your vehicle during a winter blizzard is the absolute key to survival.", "start": 57.68, "end": 60.46}, 